        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "93051e88-c2a7-59de-a50f-91a4b6930618",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Bonfire, Back in Black, Live from the Atlantic Studios\n- People: Bon Scott, Robert John \"Mutt\" Lange\n- Companies: Albert Productions, Atlantic Records\n- Organizations: AC/DC\n- Topics: album releases, box sets, tribute releases, remastering\n\nFacts:\n- Back in Black was produced by Robert John \"Mutt\" Lange and released on 25 July 1980 by Albert Productions and Atlantic Records.\n- Bonfire is a five-disc box set by AC/DC that was released in 1997.\n- Bonfire was created as a tribute to AC/DC's earlier singer Bon Scott.\n- Bonfire included the two-disc soundtrack to the movie Let There Be Rock, some early unreleased tracks, a live recording from the Atlantic Records studio in New York, and a remastered version of Back in Black.\n- Live from the Atlantic Studios is a live album by AC/DC that was released on the Bonfire box set.\n- Bonfire was remastered and released in Digipak format in 2003.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
